# Audio enum helpers: get_audio_channels, get_audio_bytes_per_channel, is_audio_planar, get_audio_planes,
# get_audio_size (bytes of ONE plane: planar => 1 channel), get_total_audio_size (all channels).
# Command: ainfo FORMAT SPEAKERS FRAMES.  Formats: 0 UNKNOWN 1 U8BIT 2 16BIT 3 32BIT 4 FLOAT 5..8 the same planar.
# Speakers: 0 UNKNOWN 1 MONO 2 STEREO 3 2.1 4 4.0 5 4.1 6 5.1 8 7.1. Values 7, 9 and 99 are not layouts => 0 channels.
# FORMAT 3 (32BIT) is 4 bytes; U8BIT is unsigned 8 bits.
ainfo 0 2 480
ainfo 1 2 480
ainfo 2 2 480
ainfo 3 2 480
ainfo 4 2 480
ainfo 5 2 480
ainfo 6 2 480
ainfo 7 2 480
ainfo 8 2 480
# all speaker layouts with a planar and an interleaved format
ainfo 4 0 1024
ainfo 8 0 1024
ainfo 4 1 1024
ainfo 8 1 1024
ainfo 4 2 1024
ainfo 8 2 1024
ainfo 4 3 1024
ainfo 8 3 1024
ainfo 4 4 1024
ainfo 8 4 1024
ainfo 4 5 1024
ainfo 8 5 1024
ainfo 4 6 1024
ainfo 8 6 1024
ainfo 4 7 1024
ainfo 8 7 1024
ainfo 4 8 1024
ainfo 8 8 1024
ainfo 4 9 1024
ainfo 8 9 1024
ainfo 4 99 1024
ainfo 8 99 1024
# unknown format values and zero frames
ainfo 9 2 100
ainfo 99 2 100
ainfo 4 2 0
ainfo 2 8 1
# size arithmetic is size_t but the product starts from uint32 frames: 0xffffffff frames of 7.1 float
ainfo 4 8 0xffffffff
ainfo 8 8 0xffffffff
